@startuml UC5_Validate_Schema_Completeness
!theme plain
title C4 Level 4 — Code Diagram: UC5 Validate Schema & Completeness


package "ADAPT iPaaS Middleware (Golang)" {
    class IngestHandler <<struct>> {
        + validator: ValidationModule
        + mongoRepo: MongoDBRepository
        + HandleIngest(w: ResponseWriter, r: Request)
    }

    class ValidationModule <<struct>> {
        + fhirValidator: FHIRValidator
        + hl7Validator: HL7Validator
        + ValidateTransformation(data: String, direction: String): ValidationResult
    }

    class FHIRValidator <<struct>> {
        + validateFHIR(data: String): ValidationResult
    }

    class HL7Validator <<struct>> {
        + validateHL7(data: String): ValidationResult
    }

    class ValidationResult <<struct>> {
        + Valid: bool
        + Errors: []string
    }

    class MongoDBRepository <<struct>> {
        + UpdateStatusQuarantined(txID: String, errMessage: String)
    }
}

IngestHandler --> ValidationModule : calls ValidateTransformation()
ValidationModule --> FHIRValidator : if direction == 'HL7V2_TO_FHIR_R4'
ValidationModule --> HL7Validator : if direction == 'FHIR_R4_TO_HL7V2'
FHIRValidator ..> ValidationResult : returns
HL7Validator ..> ValidationResult : returns
ValidationModule ..> ValidationResult : returns
IngestHandler --> MongoDBRepository : if !Valid, updates to QUARANTINED

note right of ValidationModule
  Entry point. Reads direction string to determine target format.
  Routes to validateFHIR() or validateHL7().
end note

note right of FHIRValidator
  Checks required FHIR R4 Bundle fields:
  - resourceType === 'Bundle'
  - entry[].resource.resourceType present
  - Patient fields
end note

note right of HL7Validator
  Checks required HL7v2 payload fields:
  - MSH segment
  - PID segment
  - patient_id, patient_name, date_of_birth
end note

note top of IngestHandler
  This use case is an <<include>> of UC6: Translate Data.
  Triggered automatically inside POST /api/v1/ingest after AI transformation completes.
  On failure: HTTP 400, status set to QUARANTINED in MongoDB.
end note

@enduml
